      "20 g scoop is small for a post-workout plant shake",
      "Contains sucralose in the US formula",
      "No sport certification we could find"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The Huel to buy if you want a protein shake, not a meal, and do not need certification.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "20 g per 29 g scoop (label)",
      "Calories": "About 110",
      "Third-party testing": "No sport certification found",
      "Best for": "Vegan shakes between meals"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09LNVYZX7"
  },
  {
    "id": "huel-black-edition",
    "name": "Huel Black Edition",
    "brand": "Huel",
    "badge": "Best Huel Meal",
    "category": "High-protein complete meal powder",
    "description": "Black Edition is a nutritionally complete meal powder, not a protein supplement. Huel's label lists a 90 g serving with 40 g of protein from pea and brown rice, about 390-400 calories, 28 g of carbohydrate, fiber that varies by flavor and 27 vitamins and minerals. It is sweetened with stevia and a little coconut sugar, with no artificial sweeteners, and comes in 17-meal bags.",
    "pros": [
      "40 g of plant protein per meal, per the label",
      "No artificial sweeteners; unflavored version available",
      "Filling, with fiber and 27 vitamins and minerals"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "About 400 calories per serving, too many for a protein top-up",
      "No sport certification we could find"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A strong meal replacement that only works as a protein shake if it replaces a meal.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "40 g per 90 g serving (label)",
      "Calories": "About 390-400",
      "Third-party testing": "No sport certification found",
      "Best for": "Replacing breakfast or lunch"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B085W7MZHR"
  },
  {
    "id": "huel-black-edition-ready-to-drink",
    "name": "Huel Black Edition Ready-to-Drink",
    "brand": "Huel",
    "badge": "Most Convenient",
    "category": "Bottled high-protein meal",
    "description": "The bottled version of Black Edition delivers 35 g of protein from pea and faba bean protein in about 400 calories per bottle, per Huel, with 27 vitamins and minerals and no artificial sweeteners. It is sold in 12-packs of 16.9 fl oz bottles. It is the easiest Huel to use on busy days and the most expensive per gram of protein.",
    "pros": [
