    ],
    "bottomLine": "Worth it for travel and hectic mornings, not as an everyday protein source.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "35 g per bottle",
      "Calories": "About 400",
      "Third-party testing": "No sport certification found",
      "Best for": "Grab-and-go meals"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H5T7MDPD"
  },
  {
    "id": "huel-daily-superblend",
    "name": "Huel Daily Superblend",
    "brand": "Huel",
    "badge": "Protein Plus Greens",
    "category": "Plant protein and greens blend",
    "description": "Daily Superblend combines 25 g of plant protein with greens, 6 g of fiber, probiotics and an adaptogen and mushroom blend in a two-scoop serving of about 250 calories, per Huel's listings. It states no artificial sweeteners and says it is third-party tested without naming a program. It suits people who want one morning shake instead of a protein and a greens powder.",
    "pros": [
      "25 g of plant protein per serving, per the label",
      "Greens, fiber and probiotics in one shake",
      "No artificial sweeteners, per the listing"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Expensive per 25 g of protein",
      "Unnamed testing program; extras are hard to evaluate"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A convenient all-in-one breakfast, but a costly way to buy protein.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "25 g per 2 scoops (label)",
      "Calories": "About 250",
      "Third-party testing": "Stated, program not named",
      "Best for": "Protein-and-greens breakfasts"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D1RJJV9Y"
  },
  {
    "id": "garden-of-life-sport-organic-plant-based-protein",
    "name": "Garden of Life Sport Organic Plant-Based Protein",
    "brand": "Garden of Life",
    "badge": "Alternative: Certified Plant Protein",
    "category": "Organic pea-based legume blend",
    "description": "If you want a plant protein shake with a certificate behind it, Garden of Life Sport is the alternative to Huel Complete Protein. Its listing states 30 g of protein per two-scoop serving from pea, navy bean, lentil and garbanzo bean, at about 160 calories, with USDA Organic and NSF Certified for Sport status and no artificial sweeteners. It costs similar or less per 25 g.",
    "pros": [
      "30 g of protein per serving, per the label",
      "NSF Certified for Sport and USDA Organic, per the listing",
      "No artificial sweeteners"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "No added vitamin and mineral blend like Huel's",
      "Buyers commonly report an earthy, thick texture"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The plant protein to choose over Huel if you need certification or a bigger dose.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "30 g per 2 scoops (label)",
      "Calories": "About 160",
      "Third-party testing": "NSF Certified for Sport (verify flavor)",
      "Best for": "Tested athletes, vegans"
    }
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/`,
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/best-of/`,
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Huel Protein Powder Review",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/huel-protein-powder-review/`,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Huel a protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Mostly not. Huel Powder and Black Edition are nutritionally complete meals with protein, carbohydrate, fat and fiber, at around 400 calories a serving. Huel Complete Protein is the brand's actual protein powder, with 20 g of protein in about 110 calories per Huel's label. If you want a protein shake rather than a meal, Complete Protein is the product to buy."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much protein is in Huel Black Edition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Huel's label lists 40 g of plant protein per 90 g serving of Black Edition powder, from pea and brown rice protein with some flaxseed, in about 390 to 400 calories. The bottled Black Edition Ready-to-drink lists 35 g per bottle. Figures can vary slightly by flavor, so check the label of the one you buy."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Huel Complete Protein good for building muscle?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can be, as part of enough total daily protein. A 20 g scoop of plant protein carries less leucine than the same amount of whey, so after training a scoop and a half, about 30 g of protein, is a sensible target. Total protein across the day and consistent training matter far more than which brand you choose."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Huel contain sucralose?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Some Huel products do. Huel's US ingredient list for Complete Protein includes sucralose. Black Edition powder and Black Edition Ready-to-drink are labelled as having no artificial sweeteners and use stevia, with a little coconut sugar in the powder. There is also an unflavored, unsweetened Black Edition. Check the specific product and flavor before buying."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Huel third-party tested?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We could not find NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Sport or Informed Choice certification for Huel's protein products at the time of writing. Huel publishes detailed formula pages, and the Daily Superblend listing says it is third-party tested without naming a program. Drug-tested athletes should choose a certified product whose status they can look up."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who owns Huel now?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Danone completed its acquisition of Huel in September 2026, after agreeing the deal in March and receiving UK competition clearance in August, per Danone and press coverage. Huel was founded in the UK in 2015 by Julian Hearn and James Collier. Huel has said its leadership team will stay in place, and the labels have not changed because of the deal so far."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Huel vs protein powder: which should I buy?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Buy a protein powder, including Huel Complete Protein, if you already eat regular meals and want an extra 20 to 30 g of protein for few calories. Buy a Huel meal, such as Black Edition, if you often skip meals and want a fast, filling replacement. The deciding question is whether you are adding protein or replacing a meal."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: SITE_NAME, url: SITE_URL },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.brand ?? product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "huel protein powder",
      "huel complete protein",
      "huel protein review",
      "huel vs protein powder"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Plant Protein Picks",
    link: "/best-plant-based-protein-powder/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Brand Review
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Label-Checked
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Huel Protein Powder <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Review</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Huel sells two very different things that both get called protein powder: a 110-calorie plant protein and a 400-calorie complete meal. We checked both labels, the cost per 25 g of protein and the testing, so you buy the one that fits.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#huel-complete-protein"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#complete-protein"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Compare the Two Powders
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">{author.name}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">{author.role}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#verdict" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Short Verdict</a>
          <a href="#range" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. What Huel Actually Sells</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Our Top Picks</a>
          <a href="#complete-protein" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Complete Protein, Label-Checked</a>
          <a href="#black-edition" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Black Edition, Label-Checked</a>
          <a href="#meal-vs-shake" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Huel vs a Protein Powder</a>
          <a href="#cost" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Cost per 25 g of Protein</a>
          <a href="#testing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Sweeteners, Testing and Ownership</a>
          <a href="#taste" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Taste, Texture and Digestion</a>
          <a href="#who" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Who Should Buy Huel, and Who Should Skip</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          If you want a protein shake, Huel Complete Protein is a decent plant option at a mid-to-premium price. If you want a meal, Black Edition is one of the better powdered meals on the market. The most common mistake is buying Black Edition as a post-workout protein shake and drinking 400 calories you did not plan for.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="verdict" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Short Verdict
          </h2>

          <p>
            Huel is a good brand with a naming problem for protein buyers. Its best-known powders, Huel Powder and Black Edition, are nutritionally complete meals, not protein supplements. Black Edition lists 40 g of plant protein per serving, which looks like an elite protein shake, but that 40 g comes packaged with roughly 400 calories, 28 g of carbohydrate and 15 g of fat, per Huel's own label for one flavor.
          </p>

          <p>
            The product most people searching for a Huel protein powder actually want is Huel Complete Protein. It is a plant protein built from pea, faba bean and brown rice protein, per Huel's current US formula page, with 20 g of protein in a 29 g scoop at about 110 calories. Huel adds 27 vitamins and minerals, which is unusual for a protein powder, and keeps sugar at 0 g.
          </p>

          <p>
            Is it any good? Complete Protein is a sound plant protein, but a 20 g scoop is on the small side, it uses sucralose in the US formula, and we could not find any sport certification. Black Edition is one of the strongest powdered meals you can buy if you want a quick, filling lunch. Neither is the cheapest way to buy plant protein; our <a href="/best-plant-based-protein-powder/">best plant-based protein powder</a> ranking covers cheaper and certified options.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE VERDICT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Buy Complete Protein for shakes, Black Edition for meals.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Complete Protein is the Huel protein powder. Black Edition is a 400-calorie meal with a big protein number. Choose by what you are replacing, not by the grams on the front of the bag.</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            One ownership note before the details. Danone completed its acquisition of Huel in September 2026, after agreeing the deal in March and receiving UK competition clearance in August. Huel has said its leadership team stays in place. Nothing on the labels has changed because of the deal so far, but it is worth watching future formula updates, as with any acquired brand.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="range" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Huel Actually Sells
          </h2>

          <p>
            Huel started in the UK in 2015, founded by Julian Hearn with nutritionist James Collier, with the idea of nutritionally complete, convenient food. That focus still shapes the range. Most Huel products are designed to replace a meal, and protein is one part of the nutrition panel rather than the whole point. That is why comparing Huel to a whey tub needs care.
          </p>

          <p>
            The current US range includes Huel Powder, the original complete meal; Black Edition, the higher-protein, lower-carb meal; Complete Protein, the dedicated protein powder; Daily Superblend, a protein and greens hybrid; and two ready-to-drink lines, the original Ready-to-drink and Black Edition Ready-to-drink. There are also greens powders, hot savory meals and an energy drink, which are outside the scope of a protein review.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Product</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Protein</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Calories</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">What it is</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Complete Protein</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">20 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 110</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Protein powder</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Black Edition powder</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">40 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 390-400</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Complete meal</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Black Edition Ready-to-drink</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">35 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 400</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Bottled meal</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Daily Superblend</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 250</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Protein and greens</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Original Ready-to-drink</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">20 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 400</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Bottled meal</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Huel sells direct through its own site, with subscriptions that cut the price, and through its official Huel Inc storefront on Amazon. Its ready-to-drink bottles have also moved into US retail, including Target, per trade coverage. On Amazon, check the seller line before you buy; the listings we checked were sold by Huel Inc, which is the safest option for freshness and authenticity.
          </p>

          <p>
            Everything in the range is plant-based and vegan, and Huel labels its products as gluten-free and non-GMO. That makes the brand a natural fit for dairy-free buyers. It also means the protein is a blend of legumes and grains rather than milk, which affects dose, digestion and amino acid profile in ways we cover below.
          </p>
        </div>

