        <div id="complete-protein" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Complete Protein, Label-Checked
          </h2>

          <p>
            Huel's US formula page for Complete Protein, using the Chocolate Fudge Brownie flavor, lists a 29 g scoop with 110 calories, 20 g of protein, 5 g of carbohydrate, 2 g of fiber, mostly from chicory, 1.8 g of fat and 0 g of sugar. It also lists 5 g of BCAAs and 9 g of essential amino acids per serving. Those are clean, lean numbers for a plant protein.
          </p>

          <p>
            The protein blend has changed over time. Huel's current US page names pea, faba bean and brown rice protein, while older material, including the Amazon listing copy we checked, names hemp, faba and pea. Blending legumes with a grain protein is a sensible way to round out the amino acid profile, since pea is low in methionine and rice is low in lysine. The change does not worry us, but check your bag's ingredients if hemp matters to you.
          </p>

          <p>
            The feature that makes Complete Protein different is the micronutrient blend. Huel adds 27 vitamins and minerals, which is why it calls the product nutritionally complete. That is useful if your diet is patchy, but it can double up with a daily multivitamin or other fortified foods. If you already take supplements, compare the totals rather than assuming more is better.
          </p>

          <p>
            The weak point is dose. A 20 g scoop of plant protein delivers less leucine than 20 g of whey, so for a post-workout shake many people would want a scoop and a half. Huel itself says Complete Protein is not meant to replace a meal. Our <a href="/best-pea-protein-powder/">best pea protein powder</a> guide explains why larger plant servings close most of the leucine gap with whey.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">Complete Protein, per 29 g Scoop</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
